<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="A sanitized home-server infrastructure case study."><title>Lessons learned · Home Server</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../index.html" aria-label="Engineering Notebook home"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h6v6H4zM14 4h6v6h-6zM4 14h6v6H4zM14 14h6v6h-6z"/></svg><span class="nav-label">Engineering Notebook</span></a><nav aria-label="Home-server navigation"><div class="home-server-links"><a href="/home-server/">Overview</a><a href="/home-server/hardware/">Hardware</a><a href="/home-server/security/">Security</a><a href="/home-server/monitoring/">Monitoring</a><a href="/home-server/backups/">Backups</a><a href="/home-server/services/">Services</a><a class="active" href="/home-server/lessons/">Lessons</a></div><a href="/projects/"><span class="nav-label">← Projects</span></a></nav></header><main><section class="intro section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">HOME SERVER / LESSONS</p><h1>Lessons learned</h1><p class="lede">The system became reliable one oddly specific problem at a time.</p><button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="feature-card"><div class="card-kicker">THE ACTUAL CURRICULUM</div><h3>The failures were the useful part.</h3><p>SSH configuration order mattered. iTerm permissions mattered. YAML indentation mattered. A service could be running while its health check failed. A backup could exist while being impossible to decrypt. A dashboard could be empty while the exporter was healthy.</p><p>The habit that helped most was simple: observe first, form one hypothesis, change one thing, and verify the runtime result. That approach turned a collection of confusing symptoms into a platform I can explain.</p></div></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE SHORT VERSION</p><h2>Build small. Measure honestly. Keep the escape hatch.</h2></div><div class="note-grid"><article class="note-card"><span>01</span><h3>Evidence beats assumptions</h3><p>Effective configuration and runtime behavior are more trustworthy than a file that looks correct.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>02</span><h3>Recovery is a feature</h3><p>Reboots, power loss, backups, and restores belong in the project plan.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>03</span><h3>Privacy is part of publishing</h3><p>Sanitize screenshots and text before sharing the engineering story publicly.</p></article></div></section></main><script is:inline src="../../scroll-cue.js"></script></body></html>